2. LibrePods (Android) — GPL-3.0-or-later
   https://github.com/kavishdevar/librepods
   Copyright (C) 2025 LibrePods contributors

   Protocol facts taken from its documentation and Android sources
   (docs/control_commands.md, docs/AAP Definitions.md,
   android/.../bluetooth/AACPManager.kt):
   - control identifiers and values (crates/pods-proto/src/control.rs)
   - listening mode configuration mask 0x1A (control.rs, packet.rs)
   - conversation detect control 0x28 (control.rs, packet.rs)
   - proximity key request 0x30 / reply 0x31 (packet.rs, ble.rs)
   - the encrypted part of the proximity advertisement (AES-128-ECB with
     the ENC key as sent, levels in bytes 1-3), the colour and connection
     bytes, the IRK byte order (android/.../BLEManager.kt,
     utils/BluetoothCryptography.kt) (ble.rs)
   - rename packet, opcode 0x1A (packet.rs)
   - device information field order, opcode 0x1D (info.rs)
   - battery status values, ear status values (message.rs, model.rs)

   Nothing is taken from the linux/rust branch of LibrePods
   (AGPL-3.0-only).


3. Our own measurements
   AirPods Pro (1st generation), product id 0x200E, A2084, firmware
   6619472, probed on 19 November 2026 (study "M0"):
   - the opening sequence and notification mask that work on this model
   - listening mode values 1 off, 2 ANC, 3 transparency, accepted in 0.6 s
   - no capabilities reply (0x02): capabilities come from the model table
   - settings reported on connect: 0x0D, 0x1B, 0x24, 0x18, 0x17, 0x1F
   - ear status 3 for a bud in the closed case, primary bud opcode 0x08
   - the two information records (0x0D, 0x04) and which holds the firmware
   - on the stem, with off, transparency and ANC enabled, the cycle
     transparency -> off -> ANC (issue #14); the cycle (0x1A) is not
     reported on connect
   Test fixtures: crates/pods-proto/tests/fixtures/ (serial numbers, MAC
   addresses, the owner's name and opcode 0x2B masked).


